MX_AUX_GAIN(2) 1
#ENDMYellow

#RingCtrl8 1
NUM_CACHED_RUNS 1
#RingCtrl9 

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#In addition to a jounce test, suspensions that are kinematically connected side-to-side require testing in roll to characterize their kinematics.
#
#For independent (not interconnected side-to-side) suspensions a roll test is performed mainly to obtain roll stiffness.
#
#Standards define roll as out-of-phase vertical motion of the wheels. As with jounce, this means equal and opposite motion because unequal motion is actually the sum of in-phase and outof-phase motions.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

